{
  "_why": "Role track for SHEET METAL, authored under docs/profiling/role-pack-authoring-guide.md as Batch 2 part two's first pack. fam_sheet_metal stays the generic ISCO-minor-721 interview and is NOT touched; this pack belongs to fam_sheet_metal_fab, which binds the NCO sheet-metal occupations directly (job_domain specificity 50 beats minor 30), so a thin-gauge fabricator gets sheet-metal depth and every other worker under 721 keeps the generic pack.",
  "_scope": "CUTTING, PUNCHING, BENDING AND FORMING THIN GAUGE -- laser, turret, press brake and shear, on MS, GI, stainless and aluminium sheet. The level ladder (Helper / Operator / Skilled) is asked as sheet_metal_level so the sheet can say which rung the man stands on. Structural plate work belongs to the welder's pack and auto-body denting to fam_sheet_metal; neither is bound here.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS sheet_metal_experience, asked FIRST, and it is SHEET_METAL_WORKER.tenureQuestionKey. It cannot be experience_years from qp_universal: phase order runs occupation_specific BEFORE universal_tail, so the universal answer does not exist yet when these items are selected -- gating on it is permanently false. Its options carry value_number ONLY. pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber, so a value_text beside the number would turn every gte gate below into a string comparison that is false forever. v2 unifies the scale with the other CEO-pack trades (Fresher = 0, below_one = 0); the fresher band is 'lte 0' here (ITI rows), while the depth rows open at gte 2/5 OR a rung that outranks the row (Track A/B recipe: years OR level).",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 48 and qp_universal@4 spends at most 18. Tier 0 is 7 items, tier 1 (sheet_metal_experience >= 2) adds 3, tier 2 (>= 5) adds 3 -- a senior walks 13, two fewer than the welder's 15. The three fresher items are gated sheet_metal_experience <= 0, so a senior never sees them and a fresher, who fails both gte gates by construction, tops out at 7 + 3 = 10.",
  "_sheet": "SECTION B IS READ OFF THE RATIFIED SHEET METAL REFERENCE RESUME (Jaswinder Singh, page 14), not invented. Its eight rows are Machines, Materials, Operations, Measuring instruments, Sheet thickness, Drawings, Nesting software and Sector worked, and every one has a question here that fills it. Operations carries SEVEN options because the page prints seven; trimming to the chip guideline's six would have dropped a row value the page shows. Sheet thickness is a BANDED single_select, the same ruling as the welder's plate: the page prints a band, and a free number would not render as one. The page's second half of that cell, '3200 mm brake', is a machine capacity no row of this pack stores -- a known capture gap, stated here because nothing prints it. This pack has no case in role-sheet-parity.render.test.ts yet.",
  "_keys": "NO DIGITS IN ANY question_key OR option_key. Both regexes are ^[a-z_]+$, and slugKey REFUSES a key with a digit at runtime even where the corpus validator historically let it through -- one such key makes the whole pack unparseable. material_worked, measuring_tools, drawing_reading and sector_worked are the SHARED keys other packs already use, deliberately: resume-degradation.ts sheds rows BY KEY (sector_worked first, material_worked trimmed) to keep a sheet on one page, and a private key would opt this trade out of that.",
  "pack_id": "qp_sheet_metal_fab",
  "version": 2,
  "family_id": "fam_sheet_metal_fab",
  "locale": "hi-IN",
  "status": "active",
  "review_note": "v2 (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Track B #5): Easy/Medium/Advanced tiers; 6-band experience; sheet-10 level ladder (Helper/Operator/Skilled/Senior/Supervisor, mandatory) + 2 separating confirms (skilled + senior self/other; supervisor by rule); machine retagged Medium (+CO2 laser, manual brake, hand-fab); NEW product row (Medium); material short-labels + hard; thickness re-banded to sheet (<1/1-3/3-6/>6mm — old bands drop, recorded cost); instrument/drawing rows retagged Advanced; nesting row expanded to sheet Q10 set + hard; NEW extra-work row (Advanced; drawing reading covered by its own row); hard rows gated years OR rung. No union extension (`skilled`/`senior` already confirm; helper/operator Lower). Deviations recorded: no shift row and no new ITI block (Track A/B precedent); sector kept as hard depth (no sheet row); dxf_import kept as history; new process-depth chips derive no new match skill (reach unchanged).",
  "_fresher": "Guideline section 11 #1: a fresher's Zone 4 is training, trade test, machines used in the ITI workshop and project work, and the History heading never renders empty. These three items are the ask half; resume-fresher-rows.ts, fed by this role's descriptor, is the render half. The KEYS are read literally by that file and must not be renamed; only the workshop VOCABULARY is trade-specific. The three prompts are the welder's verbatim, so they reuse its served text and its voice clips.",
